<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 14-APR.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 14-APR.</headline>
<text>
<p>Severe flooding is ongoing in the US North Plains, especially along the Red River near Fargo, North Dakota. Cool temperatures this week keep snowmelt slow in the region, preventing even worse flooding.  </p>
<p>Typhoon Isa, with 75 mph winds, is near 10n/155e, moving west northwest at 10 mph. Isa will continue to strengthen and will become a powerful typhoon during the next 48 to 72 hours. It may threaten Guam late in the period.  </p>
<p>There are no further emergency statements at this time.</p>
</text>
